@startuml
' Styling for a cleaner look
skinparam ParticipantPadding 20
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam NoteBorderColor #ADD1B2
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FEFECE
skinparam ArrowColor #4CAF50
skinparam LineColor #4CAF50
skinparam Shadowing false

title Device Connectivity Workflow (Detailed with API and User Interaction)

box "IoT System Backend" #LightBlue
    participant "Device" as D
    participant "Device Broker" as DB
    database "Data Store" as DS
end box

box "Application Layer" #LightGreen
    participant "API Gateway" as API
    actor "User/Frontend" as U
end box

note right of D : Sensor data, telemetry, events

' Device to Device Broker (MQTT) - Initial Connection & Availability
D -[#blue]> DB : Connect (MQTT)\n(with LWT: devices/lwt/deviceID)
activate DB


D -[#blue]> DB : Publish Availability\n(topic: devices/available/deviceID, QoS 1)
note right of D : Announces device presence & capabilities.

' Device subscribes to its status topic immediately after connect
D -[#blue]> DB : Subscribe to Status\n(topic: devices/status/deviceID, QoS 1)
note right of D : Device waits for API's status command.

DB -[#green]> API : Forward Availability\n(from subscription)
activate API
note left of API : API Gateway processes availability.

API -[#green]> DS : Insert Device Info\n(from Availability)
activate DS
DS --[#green]> API : Device Info Stored Confirmation
deactivate DS
note left of API : API now knows about the device.

API -[#purple]> U : Display Device Available\n(on Frontend)
activate U
U -[#purple]> API : User Command: Set Device Status\n(e.g., "Start Running")
deactivate U

API -[#orange]> DB : Publish Status Command\n(topic: devices/status/deviceID, payload: {status: "Running", location_id: "XYZ"})
deactivate API
DB -[#orange]> D : Deliver Status Command
deactivate DB

' Device to Device Broker (MQTT) - Status Update (in response to command)
activate D
D -[#blue]> DB : Publish Status Update\n(topic: devices/status/deviceID, QoS 1, on change)
note right of D : Device confirms its operational state (e.g., 'Running', 'Stopped').
DB -[#green]> API : Forward Status Update\n(from subscription)
note left of API : API Gateway processes/acknowledges internally.
deactivate D

note left of DB : MQTT: Data ingestion, routing, processing, device management.

' Device to API Gateway (HTTP POST) - Sensor Data
D -[#red]> API : Send Sensor Data (HTTP POST)\n(path: /influxdb/sensordata, every 5s when 'Running')
activate API
note right of API : Receives aggregated sensor data from devices.
API --[#red]> D : HTTP Response (2xx/4xx Status Code)\n(acknowledges data reception)
deactivate API

' API Gateway to Device Broker (for commands/data) - General interaction
API -[#orange]> DB : Request Data / Forward Command\n(e.g., to devices/status/deviceID for control)
activate DB
DB --[#orange]> API : Data / Command Acknowledgment
deactivate DB

@enduml
